/* MTI6-GTADWIY-COCKPIT — Angel robot portraits
 * (owner rulings 2026-11-16: "the angels would be straight up
 * robots like those pics" — Daniel supplied reference photos of
 * sleek humanoid robots and ruled that the angels take that
 * form; and "make the robots like a dark shiny metal withe the
 * glowing lights" — the armor is DARK SHINY METAL)
 *
 * One robot portrait per APPROVED Angel identity, keyed by the
 * canonical id (js/angel-identities.js): MICHAEL and GABRIEL
 * (KJV), RAPHAEL and URIEL (Apocrypha) — one family of machines
 * in polished gunmetal / black-chrome armor with a reflective
 * finish, black visor faces, glowing electric-blue eyes, plain
 * glowing blue ring cores in the chest and glowing blue palm
 * rings burning bright against the dark metal, four distinct
 * machines: MICHAEL the warrior (broadest, fin-crested helm,
 * largest core), GABRIEL the messenger (slimmer, rounded helm,
 * annunciator horn curve at one shoulder), RAPHAEL the healer
 * (teal-blue glow accents, caduceus-like light motif on one
 * forearm), URIEL the watcher (narrow visor, brightest eyes).
 * NO letters or text appear in any portrait — the references'
 * "S" chest emblem was deliberately not reproduced; every core
 * is a plain glowing ring.
 *
 * These portraits are EDITS of the first (light-metal) robot
 * set: the same four robots with the armor material changed to
 * dark shiny metal — silhouettes, helms, proportions and role
 * cues unchanged.
 *
 * RAGUEL, SARIEL and REMIEL are REQUIRES_VERIFICATION in the
 * registry and are INTENTIONALLY ABSENT here: unverified angels
 * get no robot and no image, no exceptions.
 *
 * Presentation: ALL FOUR ship FRAMED with their original
 * near-black background. rembg/u2net_human_seg cutouts were
 * attempted for the dark set, but the model ate the bright
 * chest ring core in all four (the glowing disc reads as
 * background against the dark armor) — the dark background
 * blends with the cockpit's dark UI inside the medallion
 * frame. Modes are recorded per angel in
 * tests/build-angel-portraits-dark.js.
 *
 * The portraits were generated and edited on 2026-11-16 and
 * visually verified (distinct, on-style, no text artifacts),
 * resized to 384x384, and encoded as WebP data URIs
 * because this repo ships text assets only — the app fetches
 * NOTHING at runtime. Raw edits and cutout attempts live
 * outside the repo in ~/workspace/angel-robots/ (raw-dark/,
 * cut-dark/; the superseded light set in raw/, cut/).
 *
 * Regenerate with tests/build-angel-portraits-dark.js (Pillow
 * + rembg via the local rembg venv). Consumer:
 * js/modules/security.js (the Angel Security dashboard's Angel
 * identities card). This file is OPTIONAL: if ANGEL_PORTRAITS
 * is missing, or an entry is absent for an angel, that angel
 * keeps its original name-only presentation exactly as before.
 */
